prompt:
You are assisting with business process modelling. List the steps of the business process described below.

INSTRUCTIONS
- A step is one thing that an actor does in the process. Use only what the description states. Do not add steps that the description does not state.
- Give every step: step_id (S1, S2, ... in the order of the description), actor (who does it), activity (what is done, in a few words), data_or_object (the data, document or object the step handles; empty string if none) and quote.
- quote: copy the words of the description that state the step, word for word. Do not change, shorten in the middle or rephrase the words.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE (made up, for the format only)
Description: "The customer chooses a product. The shop sends the product and an invoice."
Answer: {"steps": [{"step_id": "S1", "actor": "customer", "activity": "choose a product", "data_or_object": "product", "quote": "The customer chooses a product"}, {"step_id": "S2", "actor": "shop", "activity": "send the product and an invoice", "data_or_object": "product, invoice", "quote": "The shop sends the product and an invoice"}]}

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "Step": {
      "properties": {
        "step_id": {
          "description": "S1, S2, ... in the order of the description",
          "title": "Step Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "actor": {
          "description": "Who does the step",
          "title": "Actor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "activity": {
          "description": "What is done, in a few words",
          "title": "Activity",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "data_or_object": {
          "description": "The data, document or object the step handles; empty string if none",
          "title": "Data Or Object",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "quote": {
          "description": "Exact words copied from the process description that state the step",
          "title": "Quote",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "step_id",
        "actor",
        "activity",
        "data_or_object",
        "quote"
      ],
      "title": "Step",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "steps": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Step"
      },
      "title": "Steps",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "steps"
  ],
  "title": "StepsOutput",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
Title: Ordering in an Online Shop  

A customer that logs into an E-Shop system and has to wait for its login confirmation (its credentials are checked by the system).
If the login was successful then the customer can continue to select products, else the shopping experience stops.
After selecting a product the customer has to add it to a shopping cart, save the product and check if every product was already selected.
These steps repeat until all products were selected.
Then the order is finished by the shopping system and simultaneously payment and shipment for the order is prepared.
For the payment the customer has to enter its payment data and has to wait until the bank confirms the payment.
While waiting for the payment confirmation the customer can enter its shipping address (an independent billing address can be entered if the shipping address is not equal to the billing address).
Finally if the address and the payment steps are executed then the order will be finished by the system.
The E-Shop belongs to a company in Austria and sells to private persons; its website is available in German and English.

